---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="Colophon — Elvis Mao" description="Credits and materials behind Elvis Mao's website.">
	<main id="main" class="page-main">
		<header class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">COLOPHON</span><h1>Made of many things.</h1><p>A few of the people and tools behind this corner of the web.</p></header>
		<section class="about-block" style="max-width:760px;padding:30px 0 80px">
			<span class="eyebrow">CHARACTER MODEL</span>
			<h2>EM's dragon.</h2>
			<p>
				The character model is adapted from <a class="text-link" href="https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/novabeast-64f297c10547454ea4b83860146af56d">“novabeast” by joshuasteinhoff6</a>, licensed under <a
					class="text-link"
					href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
				>
					Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
				</a>.
			</p>
			<p>
				The cover uses the textured Novabeast FBX supplied by EM. Its open-eyed shape, UVs, native eyes, materials, and five original image maps are preserved. Lightweight head and eye controls let
				the character look toward the cursor.
			</p>
			<p>A Blink morph closes the existing eyelid surfaces, with a small eye corrective to keep the eyes behind the lids. The neutral, open-eyed appearance remains unchanged.</p>
			<span class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:48px">TYPE, ICONS & CODE</span>
			<p>
				IBM Plex Mono · Phosphor Icons · Astro · Three.js. The character-field experiments take inspiration from <a class="text-link" href="https://play.ertdfgcvb.xyz/">Andreas Gysin's ASCII Play</a>.
			</p>
			<p>The rotating globe uses simplified, public-domain land polygons from <a class="text-link" href="https://www.naturalearthdata.com/">Natural Earth</a>.</p>
		</section>
	</main>
	<Footer compact />
</Layout>
